[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
casa is installed and not yet running. To bring up the first node:

1. Copy the sample config and edit it. One node with an empty
   peers list is a standalone agent. For a cluster, set role to
   control and list the control nodes in peers:

     vi %%ETCDIR%%/casa.ucl

2. Enable and start the daemon. The first start makes /var/db/casa
   and the node's identity. casa logs to syslog through the log {}
   block of casa.ucl, facility daemon, tag casa. The shipped
   syslog.d and newsyslog entries put every casa line in
   /var/log/casa/casa.log and rotate it daily:

     service casa enable
     service casa start
     casa status
     tail -f /var/log/casa/casa.log

3. On the first control node, create the cluster. init prints a
   bootstrap token that lives 15 minutes. Then print the node's
   fingerprint, which every other node pins before it speaks:

     casa cluster init
     casa key show --format json

4. On each other node, join through the first one. A control node
   joins as a voter, an agent as a managed host:

     casa cluster join "[addr]:51802" --token <token> --fingerprint <fp>
     casa cluster status

%%DOCSDIR%%/USAGE.md walks through a three node cluster, an operator
key and the first policy. casa(1) lists every command.
EOM
}
]
